      {
        "id": 8371,
        "name": "VicDiGital",
        "username": "VicDiGital",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/vicdigital/{size}/2552_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-07-21T13:32:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Here's how we've been playing Apostate. &nbsp;Please let me know if we have been doing it correctly.</p><p>Apostate's relics say \"Apostate does X damage\". &nbsp;So for the purposes of certain targeting, or preventing damage from targets, would those relics count as targets or Apostate? &nbsp;We've been playing it that Apostate is the target. &nbsp;Not talking about when we attack targets, but more when certain effects reference the source of an attack. &nbsp; I'm sorry that I don't remember the exact cards we were using where this came up, but it involved either Bunker or Fanatic. &nbsp;Similarly, whenever Fanatic took damage from a relic-based power, we added +1 to it for Apostate's nemesis effect. &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:53.011Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 30.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 8370,
        "topic_slug": "apostates-relics",
        "display_username": "VicDiGital",
        "primary_group_name": null,
